their research into the ancient  relics in the courtyards of hyrule  castle  however around sunset the piece is  abruptly disturbed  a maelstrom of violent red clouds dark  in the air over the settlement  together with lightning bolts tearing  through the skies above  and from the depths of hyrule castle  itself an ominous spectre arises  soaring around the peaks of hyrule's  royal home  after years of preparation and prophecy  the day of ganon's return has finally  arrived  confident that the champions will adhere  to their duties and make their way to  the divine beasts as soon as possible  rome orders his knights to get ready to  fight alongside the sheikah's  technological wonders  as the royal guards prepare to defend  their king with their lives  this is what they prepared for in the  many years leading up to this moment  they are ready to subdue calamity ganon  the same way that their ancestors from  10 000 years ago did so successfully in  the past  but ganon gannon is cunning  what the leaders of the kingdom didn't  account for was that the calamity gannon  wasn't about to fall for the same trick  twice and instead has its own strategy  in place to foil the hylian's plan  with a deafening roar the demon king  releases numerous strands of malice  aimed at the very technology which was  designed to suppress it  before the hylians and chica realise  what has just happened  their precious machines spring to life  eyes  burning with the eerie glow of ganon's  hatred  in the blink of an eye the thriving  hyrule castle  is turned into nothing more than a  slaughterhouse with guardians cutting  down  anything in their path without  hesitation five  giant pillars which were rumored to  reside somewhere in the depths below  hyrule castle  yet had eluded the research teams  despite vigorous excavations  rose up from the ground as if reacting  to ganon's presence  each one pouring out more guardians to  do his bidding  but the cruel fate of hyrule castle its  guards  advisors poets and so many more  is only the beginning from this point on  ganon's newfound army is set on  only one thing destroying the kingdom of  hyrule  and everyone in it  unlike most of the characters we've  covered so far the fate of the last king  of hyrule  is one that is in large part left up to  our imaginations  the game itself never makes any  suggestions as to his fate beyond the  fact that he lost his life during the  calamity  creating a champion does have some  mentions but the information itself can  be quite contradictory  some parts hint that he died as soon as  the guardians besieged hyrule castle  other sections suggest that he may have  survived at least until the divine  beasts were taken over which doesn't  happen  until later down the line if the former  turns out to be the case  that would mean the video ends right  here king rome dies at the castle  the end however there are hints that  rome may have played a bigger role  during this fateful day  the biggest clue we have that suggests  the king's possible escape  is the location of his grave on the  great plateau which in the actual  in-game  files can be found under the name field  object king's tomb  a if he did die at the castle it's  unlikely that his body would be found  amidst all the chaos and patrolling  guardians  not to mention carried all the way to  this remote mountaintop  so let's sketch the most likely  alternative scenario instead  if king rome did indeed manage to escape  from hyrule castle there is a chance  that this might be a playable section  where the king with the delegation of  his best knights and royal guards fight  their way out of the castle  and into castle town all the while  trying to buy enough time for some of  the civilians to escape the turmoil  armed with his royal claymore the king  could fight his way from the castle onto  the town square  and from there he will eventually make  his way onto the fields of central  hyrule  rome commands the lion's share of his  army at hyrule castle to escort the  surviving population through the east  gate and following the road towards  akala citadel meanwhile he and his  delegation set out for hyrule garrison  since link and zelda entered the castle  through the main gate it's possible that  they may have run into the king  and it was he who ordered his daughter  to make her way to the safe haven at his  [ __ ] rico village  in the meantime rome himself takes  responsibility for the defense of  central hyrule and exits castle town  past the sacred ground mabe village and  towards hyrule garrison  the first true line of defense to the  south of the castle  unlike the ranch the quarry and mabe  village which are mostly occupied by  civilians  soldiers are stationed here and it shows  the ruins of hyrule garrison are  littered with dead and incapacitated  guardians  indicating that the forces stationed  here fought back valiantly  in war even an inevitable defeat can  still serve as a small victory and the  battle at hyrule garrison will prove to  be an important one  this defense could serve as a gameplay  section for the king  since if you remember from lincoln  zelda's journey an evacuation line was  set up from the hyrule exchange  located right below hyrule garrison all  the way towards hateno village  it's highly likely that if rome was  indeed present at the defense of hyrule  garrison  it was none other than him who ordered  it while he and the soldiers fight back  the hordes of guardians rushing from the  main capital they buy the evacuees some  time to get as many to safety as  possible  the defense at hyrule garrison won't  last for long however  with more and more guardians pouring  into the fields of central hyrule  the stronghold will eventually be  overrun and the royal knights and guards  under the command of their king will  have to abandon their efforts and  retreat back to the foot  of the great plateau and the many  outposts located alongside it  here the defense of the evacuation line  continues and it's possible that this is  an extension of the gameplay scenario  mentioned earlier  but this effort too will do nothing more  than buy some additional time  the sheer amount of guardians and their  technological superiority  can only be held back for so long this  defensive line too will  eventually fall the majority of the army  stationed at the outpost will accompany  the evacuees towards nekluda to ensure a  safe passage  meanwhile rome and the leftovers of  central hyrule's army retreat further  back  onto the great plateau itself and  towards the temple of time  and eastern abbey the ruins of the great  plateau reveal that its entrance a grand  staircase leading up to the plateau has  completely collapsed  and in the 100 years following the  events of the calamity flooded with  water  turning it into a small pond though it  is never confirmed  many have speculated that the collapse  of the entrance may have been the  hylians doing  and even creating a champion makes a  reference to this stating that it's  possible that the gate leading to the  great plateau may have been blocked to  hinder any further  guardian incursion the demolition of the  plateau's grand staircase gives a clear  insight into just how  dire the situation was that day  demolishing the only entrance to their  most holy of sights  essentially cutting themselves off from  the rest of the kingdom  here king rome and his forces prepare to  make their final stand against ganon's  central army  the soldiers stationed themselves at the  temple of time  while a small sub-group of them get  ready to defend the monks at the eastern  abbey  at the temple of time archers are  stationed on the upper floor  overseeing the fields below additionally  soldiers are stationed inside the three  buildings in front of the temple  to absorb the first wave of automata  rushing in  if these structures are eventually  overrun the surviving forces will be  able to retreat back  up the staircase and into the main  building given his importance as the  monarch of hyrule  king rome himself is likely stationed  inside the main building as well  under the protection of whatever is left  of his royal guards  while the hylians prepare for their  final stand guardians  claw their way up the walls of the great  plateau the destruction of the main  entrance  only bought them some extra time to  prepare although we never see the  guardian stalkers climb in the actual  game  probably just for gameplay reasons we  know for a fact that they  are able to ascend even the steepest of  walls  this is evident from one of the first  cutscenes in the game  the memory of a hundred years ago told  by the spirit of king rome himself  here we can see one of the machines  scaling a church at a 90 degree  angle as the guardians reach the top of  the great plateau's walls  they rush towards the temple of time  with no hesitation  as archers let loose volleys of arrows  in an attempt to slow them down  the three frontal buildings are quickly  overrun though some of the soldiers  stationed here did manage to take out  some of the machines before retreating  up to the main structure  hordes of guardians slam into the walls  of the temple of time like  waves on rock attempting to claw their  way up to reach the upper levels of the  compound  the narrow entrance to the temple likely  prevented the large-bodied guardians  easily  accessing the inside with the advantage  of their elevation  the archers successfully managed to keep  the machines at bay  who by this point are piling onto one  another in a desperate attempt to scale  the walls of this holy site  with more and more dead guardians piling  up  they'll need to find a way inside the  structure sooner or later  the front of the temple has thick and  sturdy walls  however the ruins of the temple of time  reveal its greatest weakness  the eastern wall as well as its rooftop  it's possible that the guardians circled  around to the side of the building and  concentrated their combined firepower on  this section  alternatively ganon could have even used  one of the corrupted divine beasts  aiming its devastating laser at the  temple and blasting away the eastern  wall  with the temple now breached the  guardians are now free to enter at will  wiping out the remaining survivors held  up inside  the eastern abbey has also come under  siege and although its ruins reveal a  courageous defense  with many guardian corpses littering its  interior and exterior  the abbey too is ultimately lost along  with its inhabitants  so that's it right with the guardians  now having free reign over the temple of  time  this undoubtedly signals the death of  king rome as well  well there is one additional piece of  environmental storytelling which could  hand towards one final desperation  attempt to get rome to safety  remember this is the king of hyrule  we're talking about  the soldiers and guards of the kingdom  are tasked to protect his majesty's life  at all cost it's possible that when the  temple was breached from the east side  the king and some of his guards snuck  out through the main entrance to flee  towards the mountains to the west  the reason why this might be the case is  because alongside the river of the dead  close to the bridge crossing into the  mountains we find  two additional dead guardians lying in  front of what seems to be the ruins of a  gate  there is no reason for guardians to be  present here since there are no other  hylian strongholds or settlements  situated in this area  of the plateau nothing beyond the temple  of time and eastern abbey  this could very well be the exact  location where the king  ultimately met his demise they fled  towards the mountains from the temple of  time  until they were finally cut down by  pursuing guardians  taking two of them out in a last effort  to save their beloved king  this could explain why rome's grave is  located on the top 